balance |\n| 3 | 1.05 | ≈6900–6970 | ≈16480 | Extra stock costs more than the shortages it avoids |\n| 6 | ≈ cand. 3 + bigger day 0 | ≈6910 | ≈16480 | Slightly better than 3 |\n| 5 | 1.15 | ≈7300 | worse | High holding, surplus left at the end |\n| 0 | 1.26 | worse | worse | Even more surplus; stock grows to near the 212 capacity |\n\n**Batched candidates:**\n- **Candidate 2** (every 2 days) saves about 550 in ordering fees. That roughly cancels against the cost of holding a second day's stock for good 1 (about 20 units on average, ≈520). Both goods often arrive on the same day (days 18, 22, 24, 26), so with buffer stock the morning total exceeds 212. Good 1 is accepted second, so it is the one lost (already paid for, then more shortage). That puts it below candidate 3.\n- **Candidate 4** (every 3 days) saves about 750 in fees. Extra holding costs about 1300. Overflow on days 17 and 23 (about 230 units against a 212 limit) wastes good 1. On days 26–27 only 125 units of good 1 arrive for about 150 of demand. Worst overall.\n\n**Robustness:** candidate 1 beats 7 when demand runs high (driven mainly by good 0) and loses when demand runs low. Candidates 3 and 6 are about 400 behind. The others trail by much more."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3834, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2304, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3834}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-19T07:28:11.985Z", "request_id": "req_011CgBCKf48ngaZg7J7cRpED"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"